ssion. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115:   1. 【61†readwiseio】\nL116:   2. 【62†readwise-skills】\nL117: ## Repository navigation\nL118: \nL119:   *   * 【62†Code】\nL120:   * 【63†Issues2 (2)】\nL121:   * 【64†Pull requests3 (3)】\nL122:   * 【65†Actions】\nL123:   * 【66†Projects】\nL124:   * 【67†Security and quality】\nL125:   * 【68†Insights】\nL126: \nL127: More items\nL128: \nL129: ## Files Expand file tree\nL130: \nL131: master\nL132: \nL133: ## Breadcrumbs\nL134: \nL135:   1. 【69†readwise-skills】\nL136:   2. /【70†skills】\nL137:   3. /【71†readwise-mcp】\nL138: \nL139: /\nL140: \nL141: # SKILL.md\nL142: \nL143: Copy path\nL144: \nL145: [Input: Go to file]\nL146: \nL147: Blame More file actions\nL148: \nL149: Blame More file actions\nL150: \nL151: ## Latest commit\nL152: \nL153: \nL154: \nL155: ## History\nL156: \nL157: History\nL158: \nL159: master\nL160: ## Breadcrumbs\nL161: \nL162:   1. 【69†readwise-skills】\nL163:   2. /【70†skills】\nL164:   3. /【71†readwise-mcp】\nL165: \nL166: /\nL167: \nL168: # SKILL.md\nL169: \nL170: Copy path\nL171: \nL172: Top\nL173: \nL174: ## File metadata and controls\nL175: \nL176:   * Preview\nL177: \nL178:   * Code\nL179: \nL180:   * Blame\nL181: \nL182: 267 lines (187 loc) · 9.6 KB\nL183: \nL184: 【72†Raw】\nL185: \nL186: Copy raw file\nL187: \nL188: Download raw file\nL189: \nL190: Outline\nL191: \nL192: Edit and raw actions\nL193: \nL194: name  | readwise-mcp\nL195: description  | How to use the Readwise MCP tools — access highlights, documents, and your entire reading library via MCP\nL196: # Readwise MCP\nL197: \nL198: Use the Readwise MCP tools to access the user's Readwise highlights and Reader documents. Readwise has two products:\nL199: \nL200:   * Readwise — highlights from books, articles, podcasts, and more. Includes daily review and spaced repetition.\nL201:   * Reader — a read-later app for saving and reading articles, PDFs, EPUBs, RSS feeds, emails, tweets, and videos.\nL202: ## Setup\nL203: \nL204: Add the Readwise MCP server to your client's configuration:\nL205: \nL206:     {\nL207:       \"readwise\": {\nL208:         \"type\": \"http\",\nL209:         \"url\": \"https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp\"\nL210:       }\nL211:     }\nL212: \nL213: The server handles authentication via OAuth — the user will be prompted to authorize on first use.\nL214: \nL215: ## Tool Reference\nL216: \nL217: All tools are prefixed with `mcp__readwise__`. Each tool name maps directly to a Readwise or Reader API action.\nL218: \nL219: ## Reader Tools\nL220: ### Searching documents\nL221: \nL222:     `reader_search_documents(query=\"spaced repetition\")\nL223:     `\nL224: Hybrid search (semantic + keyword) across all saved documents. Combine with filters to narrow results:\nL225: \nL226:     `# Search articles saved for later\nL227:     reader_search_documents(query=\"machine learning\", category_in=[\"article\"], location_in=[\"later\", \"shortlist\"])\nL228: \nL229:     # Search by author\nL230:     reader_search_documents(query=\"AI agents\", author_search=\"Simon Willison\")\nL231: \nL232:     # Search within a date range\nL233:     reader_search_documents(query=\"transformers\", published_date_gt=\"2024-01-01\")\nL234:     # Search by tags\nL235:     reader_search_documents(query=\"productivity\", tags_in=[\"research\"])\nL236:     `\nL237: Other filters: `title_search`, `summary_search`, `note_search`, `url_search`, `source_search`, `document_id`, `limit` (default 20, max 100).\nL238: ### Browsing documents\nL239: \nL240:     `# List 10 most recent inbox items with minimal fields\nL241:     reader_list_documents(location=\"new\", limit=10, response_fields=[\"title\", \"author\", \"summary\", \"word_count\", \"category\", \"saved_at\"])\nL242: \nL243:     # Archived articles with a specific tag\nL244:     reader_list_documents(location=\"archive\", tag=[\"research\"], category=\"article\")\nL245: \nL246:     # Unseen inbox items\nL247:     reader_list_documents(location=\"new\", seen=false)\nL248: \nL249:     # RSS feed items\nL250:     reader_list_documents(location=\"feed\", limit=20, response_fields=[\"title\", \"author\", \"summary\", \"site_name\"])\nL251: \nL252:     # Get a specific document by ID\nL253:     reader_list_documents(id=\"<document_id>\")\nL254: \nL255:     # Paginate through results\nL256:     reader_list_documents(location=\"later\", limit=10, page_cursor=\"<cursor_from_previous_response>\")\nL257:     `\nL258: Locations: `new` (inbox), `later`, `shortlist`, `archive`, `feed`. When the user says \"inbox\", use `new`. Only use `feed` when the user explicitly asks about RSS/feeds.\nL259: Use `response_fields` to limit returned data and save tokens. The `id` field is always included. Available fields: `url`, `title`, `author`, `source`, `category`, `location`, `tags`, `site_name`, `word_count`, `reading_time`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `published_date`, `summary`, `image_url`, `content`, `source_url`, `notes`, `parent_id`, `reading_progress`, `first_opened_at`, `last_opened_at`, `saved_at`, `last_moved_at`, `html_content`, `is_deleted`.\nL260: Tip: unseen documents have `first_opened_at=null`. Mark as seen via `reader_bulk_edit_document_metadata`.\nL261: ### Reading and highlighting\nL262: \nL263:     `# Get full document details including Markdown content\nL264:     reader_get_document_details(document_id=\"<id>\")\nL265: \nL266:     # Get all highlights on a document\nL267:     reader_get_document_highlights(document_id=\"<id>\")\nL268: \nL269:     # Create a highlight — html_content must match the document's HTML exactly\nL270:     # Get the HTML via reader_list_documents with response_fields=[\"html_content\"]\nL271:     reader_create_highlight(document_id=\"<id>\", html_content=\"<p>The exact passage to highlight</p>\")\nL272: \nL273:     # Highlight with a note and tags\nL274:     reader_create_highlight(document_id=\"<id>\", html_content=\"<p>Key insight</p>\", note=\"Connects to spaced repetition\", tags=[\"review\", \"concept\"])\nL275:     `\nL276: ### Saving documents\nL277: \nL278:     `# Save a URL — Reader scrapes it automatically\nL279:     reader_create_document(url=\"https://example.com/article\")\nL280: \nL281:     # Save with metadata and tags\nL282:     reader_create_document(url=\"https://example.com\", title=\"Great Article\", tags=[\"research\", \"ai\"], notes=\"Recommended by Alice\")\nL283: \nL284:     # Save raw Markdown content (provide a unique URL as identifier)\nL285:     reader_create_document(title=\"Meeting Notes\", markdown=\"# Notes from today...\", url=\"https://me.com#notes-march-2025\")\nL286:     `\nL287: ### Organizing\nL288: \nL289:     `# Move documents between locations (max 50 per call)\nL290:     reader_move_documents(document_ids=[\"<id1>\", \"<id2>\"], location=\"archive\")\nL291: \nL292:     # Bulk mark documents as seen\nL293:     reader_bulk_edit_document_metadata(documents=[{\"document_id\": \"<id>\", \"seen\": true}])\nL294: \nL295:     # Bulk update metadata\nL296:     reader_bulk_edit_document_metadata(documents=[{\"document_id\": \"<id>\", \"title\": \"Better Title\", \"tags\": [\"ai\", \"research\"]}])\nL297:     `\nL298: Note: `reader_move_documents` and `reader_bulk_edit_document_metadata` share a rate limit of 20 calls/minute. Batch document IDs into fewer calls.\nL299: ### Tags\nL300: \nL301:     `# List all tags\nL302:     reader_list_tags()\nL303: \nL304:     # Add tags to a document\nL305:     reader_add_tags_to_document(document_id=\"<id>\", tag_names=[\"important\", \"research\"])\nL306: \nL307:     # Remove tags from a document\nL308:     reader_remove_tags_from_document(document_id=\"<id>\", tag_names=[\"old-tag\"])\nL309: \nL310:     # Add tags to a highlight\nL311:     reader_add_tags_to_highlight(document_id=\"<id>\", highlight_document_id=\"<hid>\", tag_names=[\"concept\"])\nL312: \nL313:     # Remove tags from a highlight\nL314:     reader_remove_tags_from_highlight(document_id=\"<id>\", highlight_document_id=\"<hid>\", tag_names=[\"old-tag\"])\nL315: \nL316:     # Set notes on a highlight (pass null to clear)\nL317:     reader_set_highlight_notes(document_id=\"<id>\", highlight_document_id=\"<hid>\", notes=\"My updated note\")\nL318:     `\nL319: ### Exporting\nL320: \nL321:     `# Export all documents as a ZIP of Markdown files (async — returns export_id)\nL322:     reader_export_documents()\nL323: \nL324:     # Delta export — only docs updated since last export\nL325:     reader_export_documents(since_updated=\"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\")\nL326: \nL327:     # Poll for completion\nL328:     reader_get_export_documents_status(export_id=\"<id>\")\nL329:     `\nL330: \nL331: Poll `reader_get_export_documents_status` until `status` is `\"completed\"`, then use the `download_url`.\nL332: \nL333: ## Readwise Tools\nL334: ### Searching highlights\nL335: \nL336:     `# Semantic search across all highlights\nL337:     readwise_search_highlights(vector_search_term=\"learning techniques\")\nL338: \nL339:     # Search with full-text filter on a specific field\nL340:     readwise_search_highlights(vector_search_term=\"memory\", full_text_queries=[{\"field_name\": \"document_title\", \"search_term\": \"psychology\"}])\nL341:     `\nL342: \nL343: Full-text query fields: `document_author`, `document_title`, `highlight_note`, `highlight_plaintext`, `highlight_tags`.\nL344: ### Browsing highlights\nL345: \nL346:     `# List 20 most recent highlights\nL347:     readwise_list_highlights(page_size=20)\nL348: \nL349:     # Highlights from a specific book\nL350:     readwise_list_highlights(book_id=12345)\nL351: \nL352:     # Highlights from the last month\nL353:     readwise_list_highlights(highlighted_at_gt=\"2025-02-01T00:00:00Z\")\nL354: \nL355:     # Paginate\nL356:     readwise_list_highlights(page_size=100, page=2)\nL357:     `\nL358: ### Creating and editing highlights\nL359: \nL360:     `# Create a highlight (matched to a book by title/author, or goes into \"Quotes\")\nL361:     readwise_create_highlights(highlights=[{\"text\": \"The key insight here\", \"title\": \"Book Title\", \"author\": \"Author Name\"}])\nL362: \nL363:     # Create multiple highlights at once\nL364:     readwise_create_highlights(highlights=[{\"text\": \"First quote\", \"title\": \"Book A\"}, {\"text\": \"Second quote\", \"title\": \"Book B\", \"note\": \"Great point\"}])\nL365: \nL366:     # Update a highlight\nL367:     readwise_update_highlight(highlight_id=12345, note=\"New note\", add_tags=[\"concept\", \"review\"], color=\"blue\")\nL368: \nL369:     # Delete a highlight\nL370:     readwise_delete_highlight(highlight_id=12345)\nL371:     `\nL372: Colors: `yellow`, `blue`, `pink`, `orange`, `green`, `purple`.\nL373: ### Daily review\nL374: \nL375:     `# Get today's spaced repetition review\nL376:     readwise_get_daily_review()\nL377:     `\nL378: \nL379: Returns highlights selected by the algorithm plus a URL for interactive review.\nL380: ## Example Workflows\nL381: \nL382: Triage the inbox: List recent saves, read each one, decide what's worth the user's time.\nL383: \nL384:     `reader_list_documents(location=\"new\", limit=10, response_fields=[\"title\", \"author\", \"summary\", \"word_count\", \"category\", \"saved_at\"])\nL385:     reader_get_document_details(document_id=\"<id>\")\nL386:     reader_move_documents(document_ids=[\"<id>\"], location=\"later\")     # worth reading\nL387:     reader_move_documents(document_ids=[\"<id>\"], location=\"archive\")   # skip\nL388:     `\nL389: Search across everything: Find all content on a topic — run both in parallel.\nL390: \nL391:     `reader_search_documents(query=\"spaced repetition\")\nL392:     readwise_search_highlights(vector_search_term=\"spaced repetition\")\nL393:     `\nL394: Quiz on a recent read: Find a finished document, get its content and highlights.\nL395: \nL396:     `reader_list_documents(location=\"archive\", limit=10, response_fields=[\"title\", \"author\", \"summary\", \"word_count\"])\nL397:     reader_get_document_details(document_id=\"<id>\")\nL398:     reader_get_document_highlights(document_id=\"<id>\")\nL399:     `\nL400: Catch up on RSS: Browse feed items, surface the best ones, mark the rest as seen.\nL401: \nL402:     `reader_list_documents(location=\"feed\", limit=20, response_fields=[\"title\", \"author\", \"summary\", \"word_count\", \"site_name\"])\nL403:     reader_bulk_edit_document_metadata(documents=[{\"document_id\": \"<id1>\", \"seen\": true}, {\"document_id\": \"<id2>\", \"seen\": true}])\nL404:     reader_move_documents(document_ids=[\"<id>\"], location=\"later\")\nL405:     `\nL406: Save and annotate: Save a URL, highlight key passages, tag and organize.\nL407: \nL408:     `reader_create_document(url=\"https://example.com/article\", tags=[\"research\"])\nL409:     reader_create_highlight(document_id=\"<id>\", html_content=\"<p>Key passage here</p>\", note=\"This connects to...\")\nL410:     reader_add_tags_to_document(document_id=\"<id>\", tag_names=[\"important\"])\nL411:     `\nL412: Build a reading recap: See what you've finished and highlighted recently.\nL413: \nL414:     `reader_list_documents(location=\"archive\", updated_after=\"2025-03-10T00:00:00Z\", response_fields=[\"title\", \"author\", \"word_count\", \"reading_progress\"])\nL415:     reader_get_document_highlights(document_id=\"<id>\")\nL416:     readwise_list_highlights(highlighted_at_gt=\"2025-03-10T00:00:00Z\", page_size=50)\nL417:     `\nL418: \nL419: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReadwise CLI - Readwise Docs (https://docs.readwise.io/tools/cli)\nciteturn1019view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.readwise.io/tools/cli\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 217\nL0: Home\nL1: \nL2: Search docs\nL3: \nL4:   * 【0†Get Started】\nL5:   * 【1†Account FAQs】\nL6:   * 【2†Changelog】\nL7:   * 【3†Blog†blog.readwise.io】\nL8:   * Email Us (hello@readwise.io)\nL9:   * 【4†Affiliate Program】\nL10:   * 【5†MCP & CLI Tools】\nL11: \nL12:   * ## MCP & CLI Tools\nL13: \nL14:     * 【5†Overview】\nL15:     * 【6†MCP Setup】\nL16:     * 【7†CLI Setup】\nL17:     * 【8†Usage Examples】\nL18: \nL19:   1. 【0†Home】\nL20: \nL21:   2. 【5†Tools】\nL22: \nL23:   3. 【7†Cli】\nL24: # Readwise CLI\nL25: \nL26: Get started at readwise.io/cli\nL27: \nL28: These docs offer detailed instructions and FAQs about the Readwise CLI, but if you're just looking for a quick setup guide to get up and running, check out our landing page at 【9†readwise.io/cli†readwise.io】.\nL29: \nL30: The Readwise CLI gives you direct access to your Readwise and Reader data from the command line. You can directly search, read, and organize your library, or let an AI agent do it for you.\nL31: 【10†Image: Readwise CLI interactive terminal interface.†readwise-assets.s3.amazonaws.com】\nL32: ## Install the Readwise CLI\nL33: \nL34: Installing the Readwise CLI only takes two commands. The login command opens your browser for OAuth.\nL35: \nL36:     npm install -g @readwise/cli\nL37:     readwise login\nL38: \nL39: \nL40: [Button: Copy]\nL41: \nL42: For scripts and headless agents, use `readwise login-with-token <your-access-token>` instead. (You can grab your token here: 【11†readwise.io/access_token†readwise.io】.)\nL43: Once installed, your agent (Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw, etc.) can use the `readwise` command. Run `readwise --help` to see everything it can do.\nL44: ## What you can do\nL45: \nL46: These are the primary building blocks available through the Readwise CLI. You can use them directly, pipe them to other tools, or let your AI agent use them for you.\nL47: \nL48: ### Search your Reader library\nL49: \nL50:     readwise reader-search-documents --query \"aggregation theory\"\nL51: \nL52: \nL53: [Button: Copy]\nL54: \nL55: ### Read a saved document (returns Markdown)\nL56: \nL57:     readwise reader-get-document-details --document-id <id>\nL58: \nL59: \nL60: [Button: Copy]\nL61: ### Save a URL to Reader\nL62: \nL63:     readwise reader-create-document --url \"https://example.com/article\"\nL64: \nL65: \nL66: [Button: Copy]\nL67: \nL68: ### Check your inbox\nL69: \nL70:     readwise reader-list-documents --location new\nL71: \nL72: \nL73: [Button: Copy]\nL74: \nL75: ### Move documents to archive, later, or shortlist\nL76: \nL77:     readwise reader-move-documents --document-ids <id>,<id> --location archive\nL78: \nL79: \nL80: [Button: Copy]\nL81: ### Search your Readwise highlights\nL82: \nL83:     readwise readwise-search-highlights --vector-search-term \"compounding\"\nL84: \nL85: \nL86: [Button: Copy]\nL87: \nL88: ### Create a highlight\nL89: \nL90:     readwise reader-create-highlight --document-id <id> --text \"The key insight is...\"\nL91: \nL92: \nL93: [Button: Copy]\nL94: \nL95: ### Tag and organize documents\nL96: \nL97:     readwise reader-add-tags-to-document --document-id <id> --tags \"ai,research\"\nL98: \nL99: \nL100: [Button: Copy]\nL101: \nL102: ### Get today's daily review\nL103: \nL104:     readwise readwise-get-daily-review\nL105: \nL106: \nL107: [Button: Copy]\nL108: ### Export your entire library as Markdown\nL109: \nL110:     readwise reader-export-documents\nL111: \nL112: \nL113: [Button: Copy]\nL114: \nL115: ## Skills\nL116: \nL117: Skills are pre-built workflows your AI agent can run. Install them with the following command:\nL118: \nL119:     npx @readwise/cli skills install claude\nL120: \nL121: \nL122: [Button: Copy]\nL123: \nL124: ### Triage\nL125: \nL126: AI walks you through your inbox one article at a time, telling you what's worth your time and why.\nL127: ### Feed Catchup\nL128: \nL129: Skim your Reader feed in batches (RSS, newsletters, Twitter digests) to pull out the gems, then mark the rest as seen.\nL130: \nL131: ### Quiz\nL132: \nL133: Test yourself on something you just read, and get graded by the AI like it's a smart colleague who also read the piece.\nL134: ### Now Reading\nL135: \nL136: Generate a \"What I'm Reading\" webpage from your library to host on your personal site.\nL137: \nL138: Looking for inspiration?\nL139: \nL140: For more ideas about what you can do with these tools, check out our 【8†usage examples】 or 【12†browse pre-built skills on GitHub†github.com】.\nL141: ## Configuration\nL142: \nL143: Manage CLI settings with the `config` command. No authentication is required.\nL144: \nL145:     readwise config show              # show all settings\nL146:     readwise config get readonly      # get a single setting\nL147:     readwise config set readonly true # enable readonly mode\nL148: \nL149: \nL150: [Button: Copy]\nL151: ### Readonly mode\nL152: \nL153: When readonly mode is on, only read-only tools (search, list, get, export) are available — write operations are hidden. This is useful when giving an agent access to your library without letting it make changes.\nL154: \nL155:     readwise config set readonly true\nL156:     readwise --refresh\nL157: \nL158: \nL159: [Button: Copy]\nL160: Disabling readonly via the CLI logs you out and requires re-authentication (`readwise login`). This prevents an agent from silently toggling readonly off and using write tools. Toggling readonly in the interactive TUI does not require re-login.\nL161: ## CLI FAQs\nL162: ### What's the difference between the CLI and the MCP server?\nL163: \nL164: They give your AI access to the same Readwise and Reader data, but in different ways.\nL165: \nL166: The CLI is a command-line tool, where you or your agent runs `readwise` commands directly in a terminal session. The 【6†MCP server】 works with apps like Claude Desktop and ChatGPT that support the Model Context Protocol, with no terminal required.\nL167: \nL168: If you're using a terminal-based agent like Claude Code or Codex, the CLI is usually the simpler option.\nL169: ### Can I use the CLI in automated scripts or CI environments?\nL170: \nL171: Yes. Use `readwise login-with-token <your-access-token>` to authenticate without a browser. You can find your access token in your 【11†Readwise account settings†readwise.io】.\nL172: \nL173: ### Does the CLI work with both Readwise and Reader?\nL174: \nL175: Yes. Commands prefixed with `readwise-` operate on your Readwise highlights library, and commands prefixed with `reader-` operate on your Reader documents. Both are available after a single login.\nL176: ## Questions?\nL177: \nL178: 【13†Image: Readwise Contact Us】\nL179: \nL180:   * Email Us hello@readwise.io\nL181:   * 【14†Follow Us@readwise†x.com】\nL182:   * 【15†Ask the Community Join us on Reddit†www.reddit.com】\nL183: \nL184: ## Have a suggestion?\nL185: \nL186: We're pretty familiar with our product, so we occasionally fall victim to the 【16†Curse of Knowledge†en.wikipedia.org】. If any part of this documentation confuses you or seems incomplete, please let us know!\nL187: \nL188: Send Feedback (hello@readwise.io)\nL189: ## On this page\nL190: \nL191:   1. ### 【17†Install the Readwise CLI】\nL192: \nL193:   2. ### 【18†What you can do】\nL194:     1. 【19†Search your Reader library】\nL195:     2. 【20†Read a saved document (returns Markdown)】\nL196:     3. 【21†Save a URL to Reader】\nL197:     4. 【22†Check your inbox】\nL198:     5. 【23†Move documents to archive, later, or shortlist】\nL199:     6. 【24†Search your Readwise highlights】\nL200:     7. 【25†Create a highlight】\nL201:     8. 【26†Tag and organize documents】\nL202:     9. 【27†Get today's daily review】\nL203:     10. 【28†Export your entire library as Markdown】\nL204:   3. ### 【29†Skills】\nL205:     1. 【30†Triage】\nL206:     2. 【31†Feed Catchup】\nL207:     3. 【32†Quiz】\nL208:     4. 【33†Now Reading】\nL209:   4. ### 【34†Configuration】\nL210: \nL211:     1. 【35†Readonly mode】\nL212:   5. ### 【36†CLI FAQs】\nL213: \nL214:     1. 【37†What's the difference between the CLI and the MCP server?】\nL215:     2. 【38†Can I use the CLI in automated scripts or CI environments?】\nL216:     3. 【39†Does the CLI work with both Readwise and Reader?】\n"
